-- Tests for the Washington module. Every expected value is read from the source, cited beside it.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `labelling-domain`
IMPORT `wa-e2shb-1170`
IMPORT `test-kit`

§ `s.2(1) -- the duty, and s.9 -- the effective date`

#ASSERT     `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` `the generator` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` `the generator` `WA: significant and reasonable` `31 January 2027`

§ `s.1(2) -- covered provider`

-- "over 1,000,000 monthly users"
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, with monthly users numbering` 1000000) `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT     `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, with monthly users numbering` 1000001) `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
-- "publicly accessible within the geographic boundaries of the state to consumers for personal use"
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, except that it` `is not accessible in Washington for personal use`) `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
-- "does not include state, local, and tribal governments"
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, except that it` `is a government`) `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`

§ `s.3(2) and s.5 -- what the chapter does not reach`

#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, except that it` `is used business-to-business`) `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, except that it` `is a video game or interactive experience product`) `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, except that it` `is used solely for upscaling, noise reduction, or compression`) `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
-- California's videogame exemption is a different fact, and does not reach Washington.
#ASSERT     `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` (`the generator, except that it` `is a non-user-generated videogame product`) `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`

§ `s.2(1) -- video, image, or audio content only`

#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `an AI-written article` `the generator` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`

§ `s.2(4) -- materially altered: each listed minor modification is never material, even if judged significant`

#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `a change to brightness, contrast, or color`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `sharpening`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `saturating`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `applying a filter`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `resizing`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `scaling`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `cropping`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `file format conversion`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `resampling`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `denoising`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `removal of background noise in audio`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`

§ `s.2(4) -- an alteration off the list is material only if judged a significant change`

#ASSERT     `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the photo with an object removed` `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the photo with an object removed` `the editor` `WA: not significant` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT     `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the photo with red-eye removed` `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the photo with red-eye removed` `the editor` `WA: not significant` `1 February 2027`
-- One listed and one unlisted alteration: the unlisted one carries it.
#ASSERT     `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` (`a photo an AI system altered by` (LIST `cropping`, `face replacement`)) `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`
-- No AI alteration at all.
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the camera capture` `the editor` `WA: significant and reasonable` `1 February 2027`

§ `s.2(1) -- "To the extent commercially and technically reasonable"`

#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1) requires the provider to include provenance data` `the AI-generated image` `the generator` (`Washington judgements: significant change` TRUE `, reasonable` FALSE) `1 February 2027`

§ `s.2(1) second sentence and s.1(4) -- provenance data that lets a user assess`

#ASSERT     `the content carries provenance data that lets a user assess whether it was created or materially altered by a generative AI system` `the AI-generated image`
#ASSERT     `the content carries provenance data that lets a user assess whether it was created or materially altered by a generative AI system` `the photo with an object removed`
#ASSERT NOT `the content carries provenance data that lets a user assess whether it was created or materially altered by a generative AI system` `the AI-generated image, stripped`
-- A camera-capture manifest says nothing about a generative AI system.
#ASSERT NOT `the content carries provenance data that lets a user assess whether it was created or materially altered by a generative AI system` `the camera capture`

§ `s.2(2) -- the C2PA safe harbour`

#ASSERT     `its provenance data is deemed compliant with section 2(2)` `the AI-generated image`
#ASSERT NOT `its provenance data is deemed compliant with section 2(2)` `the AI-generated image, stripped`
#ASSERT REFUSED `its provenance data is deemed compliant with section 2(2)` (`content of kinds` (LIST `image`) `that came to exist by` `generated by an AI system` `altered by` EMPTY `carrying` NOTHING `watermarked` TRUE)
        BECAUSE "whether this watermark follows a commonly supported technical standard is not modelled"
